Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `a` was consumed by `a.move()`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/move_mark_positions.jet:22:11
    |
 22 |     print(a.len())
    |           ^
  --> tests/ui/move_mark_positions.jet:14:21
    |
 14 |     holder: Box{xs: a.move()}
    |                     ^^^^^^ `a` moved to `a.move()` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `a` after the move, or give `a.move()` a copy with `a.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121

